## Article 315. Powers of appeal court

```catala
declaration scope Article315AppealPowers:
  input check content AppealPowersCheck
  output mayLeaveUnsatisfied content YesNo
  output mayCancelAndNewDecision content YesNo
  output mayCancelAndCloseOrLeave content YesNo
  output mayInvalidateAndClose content YesNo
  output mayCancelAndRedirect content YesNo

scope Article315AppealPowers:
# Leave complaint unsatisfied when first instance correct
  label leave_unsatisfied definition mayLeaveUnsatisfied under condition
    check.firstInstanceCorrect = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_leave definition mayLeaveUnsatisfied equals No

# Cancel and adopt new decision when cancellation ground exists
  label cancel_new definition mayCancelAndNewDecision under condition
    check.cancellationGroundExists = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel_new definition mayCancelAndNewDecision equals No

# Cancel and close or leave without consideration
  label cancel_close definition mayCancelAndCloseOrLeave under condition
    check.closureOrLeaveWithoutConsiderationGround = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel_close definition mayCancelAndCloseOrLeave equals No

# Invalidate first instance decision
  label invalidate definition mayInvalidateAndClose under condition
    check.closureOrLeaveWithoutConsiderationGround = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_invalidate definition mayInvalidateAndClose equals No

# Cancel and redirect to another court for jurisdiction
  label redirect definition mayCancelAndRedirect under condition
    check.jurisdictionViolation = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_redirect definition mayCancelAndRedirect equals No
```

## Article 316. Grounds for leaving appeal unsatisfied

```catala
declaration scope Article316LeaveUnsatisfied:
  input check content AppealPowersCheck
  output firstInstanceCorrect content YesNo

scope Article316LeaveUnsatisfied:
# First instance correct when properly established facts and applied law
  label correct definition firstInstanceCorrect under condition
    check.firstInstanceCorrect = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label incorrect definition firstInstanceCorrect equals No
```

## Article 317. Grounds for cancellation and new decision

```catala
declaration scope Article317CancellationGrounds:
  input check content AppealCancellationCheck
  output cancellationGroundExists content YesNo
  output mandatoryCancellationApplies content YesNo

scope Article317CancellationGrounds:
# Incomplete findings
  label incomplete definition cancellationGroundExists under condition
    check.cancellationGround = AppealCancellationGround.IncompleteFindings
    consequence equals Yes

# Unproven circumstances
  label unproven definition cancellationGroundExists under condition
    check.cancellationGround = AppealCancellationGround.UnprovenCircumstances
    consequence equals Yes

# Conclusions dont match circumstances
  label mismatch definition cancellationGroundExists under condition
    check.cancellationGround = AppealCancellationGround.ConclusionsDontMatchCircumstances
    consequence equals Yes

# Wrong substantive law
  label wrong_law definition cancellationGroundExists under condition
    check.cancellationGround = AppealCancellationGround.WrongSubstantiveLaw
    consequence equals Yes

# Procedural violation
  label procedural definition cancellationGroundExists under condition
    check.cancellationGround = AppealCancellationGround.ProceduralViolation
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_ground definition cancellationGroundExists equals No

# Mandatory cancellation for specific procedural violations
  label unauthorized_composition definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryViolation = MandatoryProceduralViolation.UnauthorizedCourtComposition
    consequence equals Yes

  label recused_judge definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryViolation = MandatoryProceduralViolation.JudgeShouldHaveBeenRecused
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_notified definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryViolation = MandatoryProceduralViolation.ParticipantNotProperlyNotified
    consequence equals Yes

  label non_participant definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryViolation = MandatoryProceduralViolation.RightsOfNonParticipantAffected
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_signed definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryViolation = MandatoryProceduralViolation.DecisionNotSigned
    consequence equals Yes

  label wrong_judges definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryViolation = MandatoryProceduralViolation.DecisionByWrongJudges
    consequence equals Yes

  label simplified_instead_general definition mandatoryCancellationApplies under condition
    check.mandatoryViolation = MandatoryProceduralViolation.SimplifiedUsedInsteadOfGeneral
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_mandatory definition mandatoryCancellationApplies equals No
```

## Article 318. Grounds for redirecting to another court

```catala
declaration scope Article318RedirectToAnotherCourt:
  input check content AppealRedirectCheck
  output redirectForJurisdictionViolation content YesNo

scope Article318RedirectToAnotherCourt:
# Redirect when jurisdiction violated
  label redirect definition redirectForJurisdictionViolation under condition
    check.jurisdictionViolation = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# No redirect for territorial jurisdiction if appellant did not raise it
  label no_redirect_excused definition redirectForJurisdictionViolation under condition
    check.territorialJurisdictionViolation = Yes
    and check.appellantDidNotRaiseJurisdiction = Yes
    and check.appellantHadGoodCause = No
    consequence equals No

  label no_redirect definition redirectForJurisdictionViolation equals No
```

## Article 319. Grounds for cancellation with closure or leave without consideration

```catala
declaration scope Article319CancellationWithClosure:
  input check content AppealClosureWithRedirectCheck
  output mustCancelAndClose content YesNo
  output administrativeJurisdictionViolationMandatory content YesNo

scope Article319CancellationWithClosure:
# Cancel and close when closure or leave ground exists
  label cancel_close definition mustCancelAndClose under condition
    check.closureOrLeaveGroundExists = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel definition mustCancelAndClose equals No

# Administrative jurisdiction violation is mandatory ground regardless of complaint grounds
  label mandatory definition administrativeJurisdictionViolationMandatory under condition
    check.administrativeJurisdictionViolation = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_mandatory definition administrativeJurisdictionViolationMandatory equals No
```

## Article 320. Grounds for cancelling obstructing ruling

```catala
declaration scope Article320CancelObstructingRuling:
  input check content AppealCancelRulingCheck
  output rulingMustBeCancelled content YesNo

scope Article320CancelObstructingRuling:
# Cancel ruling that obstructs further proceeding
  label cancel definition rulingMustBeCancelled under condition
    check.rulingObstructsProceeding = Yes
    and (check.incompleteFindings = Yes
    or check.unprovenCircumstances = Yes
    or check.conclusionsDontMatchCircumstances = Yes
    or check.wrongLawOrProceduralViolation = Yes)
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_cancel definition rulingMustBeCancelled equals No
```

## Article 321. Appeal court decisions

```catala
declaration scope Article321AppealDecisions:
  output decisionsInFormOfPostanova content YesNo
  output proceduralQuestionsByRulings content YesNo
  output decisionsSubjectToCassation content YesNo

scope Article321AppealDecisions:
# Appeal court decisions in form of postanova
  label postanova definition decisionsInFormOfPostanova equals Yes

# Procedural questions resolved by rulings
  label rulings definition proceduralQuestionsByRulings equals Yes

# Appeal decisions subject to cassation
  label cassation definition decisionsSubjectToCassation equals Yes
```

## Article 322. Content of appeal court postanova

```catala
declaration scope Article322PostanovaContent:
  output mustContainIntroductoryPart content YesNo
  output mustContainDescriptivePart content YesNo
  output mustContainMotivationalPart content YesNo
  output mustContainOperativePart content YesNo

scope Article322PostanovaContent:
# Postanova must contain all four parts
  label introductory definition mustContainIntroductoryPart equals Yes

  label descriptive definition mustContainDescriptivePart equals Yes

  label motivational definition mustContainMotivationalPart equals Yes

  label operative definition mustContainOperativePart equals Yes
```

## Article 323. Late appeal complaint

```catala
declaration scope Article323LateAppeal:
  input check content LateAppealCheck
  output lateComplaintConsidered content YesNo
  output mayStayPreviousDecisions content YesNo
  output refusalForAlreadyConsideredGrounds content YesNo

scope Article323LateAppeal:
# Late complaint considered when arrived after review and complainant not present
  label considered definition lateComplaintConsidered under condition
    check.complaintArrivedAfterReviewEnded = Yes
    and check.complainantNotPresentAtReview = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_considered definition lateComplaintConsidered equals No

# May stay previous postanova and first instance decision
  label may_stay definition mayStayPreviousDecisions under condition
    check.complaintArrivedAfterReviewEnded = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_stay definition mayStayPreviousDecisions equals No

# Refuse when grounds already considered
  label refuse definition refusalForAlreadyConsideredGrounds under condition
    check.groundsNotPreviouslyConsidered = No
    consequence equals Yes

  label no_refuse definition refusalForAlreadyConsideredGrounds under condition
    check.groundsNotPreviouslyConsidered = Yes
    consequence equals No
```

## Article 324. Separate ruling by appeal court

```catala
declaration scope Article324AppealSeparateRuling:
  output mayIssueSeparateRuling content YesNo

scope Article324AppealSeparateRuling:
# Appeal court may issue separate ruling per Art 249 rules
  label separate_ruling definition mayIssueSeparateRuling equals Yes
```

## Article 325. Entry into force of appeal court decisions

```catala
declaration scope Article325AppealEntryIntoForce:
  input check content AppealEntryIntoForceCheck
  output postanovaEntersIntoForceOnAdoption content YesNo
  output rulingEntersIntoForceOnPronouncement content YesNo
  output rulingOutsideSessionEntersOnSignature content YesNo

scope Article325AppealEntryIntoForce:
# Postanova enters into force on adoption
  label postanova_adoption definition postanovaEntersIntoForceOnAdoption under condition
    check.isResolution = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# Ruling enters into force on pronouncement
  label ruling_pronouncement definition rulingEntersIntoForceOnPronouncement under condition
    check.isRuling = Yes
    and check.pronouncedInSession = Yes
    consequence equals Yes

# Ruling outside session or all absent or written enters on signature
  label ruling_signature definition rulingOutsideSessionEntersOnSignature under condition
    check.isRuling = Yes
    and (check.allParticipantsAbsent = Yes
    or check.isWrittenProceeding = Yes)
    consequence equals Yes

  label not_postanova definition postanovaEntersIntoForceOnAdoption equals No

  label not_ruling definition rulingEntersIntoForceOnPronouncement equals No

  label not_outside definition rulingOutsideSessionEntersOnSignature equals No
```

## Article 326. Return of administrative case

```catala
declaration scope Article326CaseReturn:
  output caseReturnedToFifteenDays content YesNo

scope Article326CaseReturn:
# Case returned to first instance within 15 days after appeal review
  label fifteen_days definition caseReturnedToFifteenDays equals Yes
```
